  ex:l4-hist-2d-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:Histogram2D ; skos:prefLabel "60 synthetic paired concentration/response observations"@en ; cd:body "60 synthetic paired concentration/response observations. Equal rectangular cells; number and color show observations per cell, not a third measured variable."@en ; cd:usesDataset ex:l4-paired-data ; cd:xAxisLabel "Concentration"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "mg/L" ; cd:yAxisLabel "Response"@en ; cd:yAxisUnit "a.u." ; cd:binEdges ex:l4-hist-2d-chart-edge-1 ; cd:yBinEdges ex:l4-hist-2d-chart-y-edge-1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-intro-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "2D histograms: bin paired measurements on two axes"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-intro-intro a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Scenario: paired measurements**\n\n60 concentration/response pairs. Keep each pair together and count observations in rectangular cells."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-intro-reading-1 a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Read a cell**\n\n- Intersection of an **x bin and a y bin**.\n- Number and color encode **count**.\n- Empty cell: **zero** observations."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-intro-reading-2 a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Do not confuse the encodings**\n\nEqual widths within each axis. ==Color is frequency, not response magnitude.== Read both axes and the count scale."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-reading-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Read a 2D histogram: an upward band, not a calibration"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-reading-intro a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Scenario**\n\nThe same 60 synthetic paired sensor readings, aggregated on a concentration–response grid."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-reading-reading-1 a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Interpretation**\n\nOccupied cells form an **upward band**: higher concentrations tend to accompany higher responses here."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-histogram-2d-reading-reading-2 a cd:Interpretation ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Limit**\n\nBinning hides exact pairs and within-cell scatter. ==Not a fitted calibration==, proof of linearity or a causal conclusion."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
